<instruction name="PUNPCKLBW/PUNPCKLWD/PUNPCKLDQ/PUNPCKLQDQ">
 <copyright>Copyright (C) Intel Corporation. All Rights Reserved.</copyright>
 <shortdesc>Unpack Low Data</shortdesc>
 <longdesc><para unique="1091851">
   <string>Unpacks and interleaves the low-order data elements (bytes, words, doublewords, and quadwords) of the destina&#173;tion operand (first operand) and source operand (second operand) into the destination operand. (</string><link linkend="21211: 05_FigureFrame: Figure 3-15. PUNPCKHBW Instruction Operation"><string>Figure&#160;4&#8209;22</string></link><string> shows the unpack operation for bytes in 64-bit operands.). The high-order data elements are ignored.</string></para>
  <table>
   <caption>Figure 4-22.  PUNPCKLBW Instruction Operation Using 64-bit Operands</caption>
